@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how proveo attributes a failure to a LAYER instead of arguing about it
' covers: e2e/ladder_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/**
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
' covers: internal/contract/agent_launch_guard_test.go
' covers: defs/**/entrypoint.sh
' What a launch must not drop: _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml.
'
' ── THE METHOD ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Start with the smallest thing that can run an agent at all — stock sbx, stock
' image, no proveo — and add exactly ONE capability per rung. Run the same
' scenario at each. The first rung that fails NAMES ITS OWNER, because it is the
' only rung that introduced anything.
'
' The alternative is what this replaces: a whole stack under test at once, a
' symptom visible only at the top, and a root cause argued from inference. That
' argument has been lost repeatedly. Three wrong root causes preceded the ladder
' for one failure, and the sequence of a debugging session is a poor instrument —
' the thing you changed last is not the thing that broke.
'
' ── THE RUNGS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   0  bare sbx agent      stock sbx agent, stock image, no proveo whatsoever
'   1  proveo base image   the harness image (-t) and nothing else
'   2  browser variant     the same, swapped for the -browser image
'   3  posture Kit + seed  proveo's allowlist, env and seed (LSPs, toolchain),
'                          plus the proveo home mounted as a workspace
'
' RUNG 0 IS THE ONE THAT MATTERS and the one nobody runs first. It answers a
' question no amount of reading proveo can: is this proveo's bug at all? A
' failure there is upstream's, and the record already holds two — sbx does not
' support CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN (sbx-releases#11) and its forward proxy
' rewrites the Authorization header on api.anthropic.com (sbx-releases#210).
' Neither is fixable here, and both would have been chased in proveo without it.
'
' RUNG 3 MOUNTS THE PROVEO HOME DELIBERATELY. The mixin points HOME at it; drop
' the mount and HOME names a path that does not exist, the agent finds no config
' and opens a first-run picker that blocks on a keypress no automation sends.
' A rung that reproduces nothing is worse than no rung.
'
' ── A DEF WITH NO BUILT-IN AGENT GETS AN EXTRA RUNG ───────────────────────
' sbx has built-in agents for claudecode, cursor and opencode; their agent name
' carries the launch. cecli has none, so it runs under the stock `shell` agent
' with its own launcher as the COMMAND.
'
' THE COMMAND IS FLAG-LEADING, AND THAT IS NOT COSMETIC. sbx's shell agent
' documents the rule: a word after `--` that BEGINS WITH A DASH is appended to
' `bash -l`, and a BARE word REPLACES it. proveo passed the bare target name, so
' `-- cecli` ran `bash cecli`; bash searched PATH, found the Python console
' script and read it as shell — `import: not found`. Nothing was absent from the
' image, and the rung looked like a packaging failure.
'
' So the command is `-c <script>` and the script EXECs the def's own
' `cecli-entrypoint`. Both halves are load-bearing: a shebang is only consulted
' on exec, so a launch that merely NAMES the binary reintroduces the same bug in
' another spelling, and skipping the def's entrypoint starts the harness without
' the rule and evidence arguments the def declares — a green rung that dropped
' the contract it was meant to measure. `bash -c` takes the word after the
' script as $0, so a placeholder sits there or the first real argument is
' swallowed silently.
'
' The COMMAND is also what makes the extra rung necessary: the def's entrypoint
' does not execute until it is added. An image rung without it measures a bare
' shell inside our image: real, but not the thing that failed. So the command is its own rung, inserted after
' the base image, and every rung above keeps it:
'
'   0  bare sbx shell     stock agent, stock image, NO command
'   1  proveo base image  the image, still no command
'   2  agent command      `-- -c '<exec cecli-entrypoint …>'` — the def's
'                         entrypoint runs from here
'   3  browser variant
'   4  posture Kit + seed
'
' Rung 0 deliberately carries no command: `cecli` does not exist in the stock
' image, so passing it there would fail for a reason that is not under test.
'
' The ladder used to SKIP these defs outright — "no sbx agent, docker only" —
' which left the one harness whose failure is still unexplained as the one the
' instrument could not reach.
'
' ── ONE HARNESS IS ONE DATA POINT ──────────────────────────────────────────
' PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET selects the def, defaulting to claudecode. It is a knob
' rather than a constant because the sbx fixes this suite proved for claudecode
' were carried to cursor by SYMMETRY, not by measurement — and a contract checked
' against one harness is a contract with one data point.
'
' The open case WAS opencode: it died IDLE on sbx with no input at all, at
' roughly startup + 30s, while cursor and claudecode survived the same wait
' (e2e/idle_test.go, SPEC: _spec/internal/sbx/sandbox-backend.puml).
'
' ── THE LADDER ANSWERED IT, AND THE ANSWER WAS OURS ────────────────────────
' Rung 0 (stock sbx, stock image) held 48s. Rung 1 (the proveo image, nothing
' else) died in 9s. cursor and claudecode already routed their launch through
' `proveo_exec_agent` and both survived the same wait — which is the whole 2x2,
' and it names the image layer rather than sbx.
'
' The defect: `"$@"` is AMBIGUOUS and the two backends disagree about what it
' holds. On docker, proveo passes the harness's own flags, which belong AFTER
' the binary. On sbx, the built-in agent kit supplies the whole COMMAND in the
' CMD position and proveo's ENTRYPOINT turns that into `"$@"`. Appending it
' blindly hands the AGENT NAME to the agent as a positional, which every harness
' reads as a prompt or a path: opencode ran `opencode opencode` and exited, the
' sbx session ended with it, and the sandbox auto-stopped 30s later as
' "sandbox ... was stopped" — an infrastructure symptom three layers from its
' cause.
'
' `proveo_exec_agent` disambiguates, and a contract test asserts every
' agent-launching def entrypoint INVOKES it (a mention in a comment does not
' count — that is exactly the state a careless edit leaves). It asserts PRESENCE
' and nothing narrower: a first attempt also rejected any bare
' `exec <agent> "$@"`, which flagged cursor's utility-subcommand passthrough —
' `login`, `logout`, `status` exec straight through with none of the autonomy
' flags, deliberately and by spec (_spec/defs/cursor/cursor-paradigm.puml). A
' guarded default launch beside a deliberate passthrough is correct, and a check
' that cannot tell them apart costs more than it catches.
'
' The mirror rule at the sbx adapter: a def WITH a built-in agent carries no
' command at all, because that agent already launches itself — adding one is
' the other way to arrive at `opencode opencode`.
title Capability ladder — add one thing per rung, and the first failure names its owner

node "rung 0 — bare sbx" as R0 <<cloud>> {
  component "stock sbx agent\nstock image · no proveo" as A0 <<app>>
}
node "rung 1 — proveo image" as R1 <<host>> {
  component "harness image (-t)" as A1 <<app>>
}
node "rung 2 — browser variant" as R2 <<host>> {
  component "-browser image" as A2 <<app>>
}
node "rung 3 — posture Kit" as R3 <<host>> {
  component "allowlist · env · seed\n+ proveo home mounted" as A3 <<app>>
}
component "the first rung that FAILS\nowns the failure" as OWNER <<error>>

A0 ARROW_MAIN A1 : + the image
A1 ARROW_MAIN A2 : + the browser layer
A2 ARROW_MAIN A3 : + proveo's posture
R0 ARROW_ERROR OWNER : upstream's bug
R1 ARROW_ERROR OWNER : the image's
R2 ARROW_ERROR OWNER : the browser layer's
R3 ARROW_ERROR OWNER : proveo's own

note bottom of R0
  **Rung 0 is the one nobody runs first.** It
  answers what reading proveo cannot: is it
  proveo's bug at all?
end note

note bottom of R0
  Two upstream failures are on record here:
  ""sbx-releases#11"" and #210. Both would have
  been chased inside proveo without this rung.
end note

note bottom of R1
  **48s at rung 0, 9s at rung 1.** The image layer
  owned it: ""$@"" handed the agent its own name,
  opencode exited, and the sandbox auto-stopped
  30s later as an infrastructure fault.
end note

note bottom of R1
  **Flag-leading, or sbx drops ""bash -l"".**
  A bare word REPLACES it, so ""-- cecli"" ran
  ""bash cecli"" — a Python console script read as
  shell. The command is ""-c"" and it execs
  the def's own entrypoint.
end note

note bottom of R3
  **The proveo home is mounted on purpose.** The
  mixin points HOME at it; without the mount the
  agent finds no config and blocks on a first-run
  picker no automation answers.
end note

note bottom of OWNER
  **One thing per rung, or the method is gone.**
  Two additions and a failure names two suspects,
  which is the position the ladder exists to
  leave.
end note

note bottom of OWNER
  ""PROVEO_LADDER_TARGET"" selects the def. The
  sbx fixes proved for claudecode reached cursor
  by symmetry, not measurement — one harness is
  one data point.
end note
@enduml
